            <ArticleTitle>Inflammatory pseudo-tumour as an unusual cause of colonic obstruction: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>462-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inflammatory pseudo-tumour (IPT), also known as inflammatory myofibroblastic tumour or plasma cell granuloma, is a benign inflammatory solid tumour that may mimic malignancy. The etiology is obscure. Lung, spleen and mesentery are common sites of involvement. Colonic occurence is rare. Herein we report a case of IPT arising from the hepatic flexura with regard to its radiological, operative and histologic findings, that lead to colonic obstruction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
